n south central Colorado...\nWest Central Costilla County in south central Colorado...\nSouth Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 400 PM MST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Conejos River, from Mogote downstream\nto Manassa, and the San Antonio River, near Ortiz downstream to\nManassa, is ongoing. Additional flooding of creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is possible. Numerous\nroads remain closed due to flooding. Expect many areas of slow\nmoving or standing water through eastern Conejos County.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 347 PM MST, Upstream runoff from recent rain and snowmelt is\ncausing flooding into eastern Conejos County.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Alamosa East, Conejos and\nOrtiz.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-04T16:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Conejos, CO; Costilla, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b092e67b29472df648ea32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b092e67b29472df648ea32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:29PM MST until November 6 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\n.Minor flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is expected due\nto upstream flooding occurring in the vicinity of Monte Vista.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon to late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 2:30 PM MST Monday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage early\nWednesday afternoon to a crest of 9.6 feet late Wednesday\nevening. It will then fall below flood stage early Thursday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-06T00:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T17:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 031720 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1020 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Windy across the plains early today. - Unsettled pattern in place through Saturday. - Drier and warmer conditions return early next week. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH TONIGHT/... Issued at 125 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 Today - Tonight: For Tuesday, relatively quiet weather","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T18:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 031812 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1112 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-041815- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosq","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T19:02:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... No meteorological fire weather concerns through the next several days across the district. An upper wave will move across the area Wednesday through Thursday morning, with accumulating snow over the Central Mountains, 